@startuml Android Activity Launch Simplified
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title Android Activity Launch Process (Simplified)

participant "Client App" as Client
participant "ActivityManagerService" as AMS
participant "Zygote" as Zygote
participant "Target App Process" as TargetApp
participant "ActivityThread" as AT
participant "Activity" as Activity
participant "WindowManager" as WM

== 1. Launch Request ==
Client -> AMS: startActivity(Intent)
AMS -> AMS: resolve Intent & check permissions

== 2. Process Creation (if needed) ==
alt Cold Start
    AMS -> Zygote: fork new process
    Zygote -> TargetApp: create process
    TargetApp -> AT: main()
    AT -> AMS: attachApplication()
end

== 3. Activity Creation ==
AMS -> AT: scheduleLaunchActivity()
AT -> AT: handleLaunchActivity()
AT -> Activity: new Activity()
AT -> Activity: attach()

== 4. Activity Lifecycle ==
AT -> Activity: onCreate()
Activity -> Activity: setContentView()
AT -> Activity: onStart()
AT -> Activity: onResume()

== 5. Window & Display ==
Activity -> WM: create window
WM -> WM: make visible
WM -> Activity: onWindowFocusChanged(true)

== 6. Complete ==
AT -> AMS: activityResumed()
note over Activity: Activity is now visible and interactive

@enduml